            <ArticleTitle>Cadmium-Free InP/ZnSeS/ZnS Heterostructure-Based Quantum Dot Light-Emitting Diodes with a ZnMgO Electron Transport Layer and a Brightness of Over 10 000 cd m-2.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/smll.201603962</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cadmium-free thick-shelled InP/ZnSeS/ZnS quantum dot (QD) was synthesized using the heating-up approach. This quantum dots was used in inverted quantum dots light emitting diode (QLED) devices. The brightness of the inverted QLED device can reach a brightness of over 10 000 cd m-2 , low turn-on voltage (2.2 V), and high power efficiency (4.32 lm W-1 ).</AbstractText>
